== ieee_16_7_overlapped_concatenation_match
# evidence: example
# §16.7 overlapped concatenation: (a ##1 b ##1 c) ##0 (d ##1 e ##1 f) is the same as a ##1 b ##1 c&&d ##1 e ##1 f; c and d are
# required at the same tick (sample 2). Here a b c&d e f at samples 0 to 4: match ends at 4.
property: go |-> (a ##1 b ##1 c) ##0 (d ##1 e ##1 f)
signals: go a b c d e f
clause: 16.7 16.12.7
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.7 overlapped concatenation example, re-expressed
sample  : 0 1 2 3 4 5
go      : 1 . . . . .
a       : 1 . . . . .
b       : . 1 . . . .
c       : . . 1 . . .
d       : . . 1 . . .
e       : . . . 1 . .
f       : . . . . 1 .
pass    : . . . . 1 .
pending: 0

== ieee_16_7_overlapped_concatenation_d_one_tick_late
# evidence: derived
# §16.7 overlapped concatenation (derived): d one tick after c is not the overlap the ##0 asks for; c&&d is false at sample 2 and
# the attempt fails there although the shifted sequence would otherwise be complete.
property: go |-> (a ##1 b ##1 c) ##0 (d ##1 e ##1 f)
signals: go a b c d e f
clause: 16.7 16.12.7
class: normative
origin: IEEE 1800-2017 §16.7 overlapped concatenation example, re-expressed
sample  : 0 1 2 3 4 5 6
go      : 1 . . . . . .
a       : 1 . . . . . .
b       : . 1 . . . . .
c       : . . 1 . . . .
d       : . . . 1 . . .
e       : . . . . 1 . .
f       : . . . . . 1 .
fail    : . . 1 . . . .
pending: 0

